      "sourceTextSha256": "c64d2e98db0fd62d89dc40a6746883e01f896d2c6c7886a9f26a28104e7291b7",
      "text": "The tour begins in the historic centre of La Paz. See the city’s main squares and architectural landmarks and learn about its history and the daily lives of its residents.\n\nThe Witches’ Market sells medicinal herbs, amulets, ritual objects and handicrafts. These items are connected to Andean beliefs that are still practised in Bolivia today.\n\nThen head to the Valley of the Moon on the outskirts of La Paz. Erosion has carved clay spires, narrow gullies and rock formations here. Light and shadow bring out the shapes that gave the valley its name.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-qkp8w5l4dosmw9l9yyz",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
    {
